7592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "aa3208c3-dd8f-52a7-9e52-31f81d41b1b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-355240" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc692d5337c00f1cca52fe3020d26a2859288c257f0a049e3f6b7f159353d7ce.png)\n\nLet $T=\\{0,1,3,4\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $g(t)$ for each $t\\in T.$ Assuming that all the dots have integer coordinates, compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}g(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}g(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}g(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}g(t)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, \n\n- the highest point is at $(0,3),$ so ${max}_{t\\in T}g(t)=3$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}g(t)=0,$ and\n\n- the lowest point is at $(4,-2),$ so ${min}_{t\\in T}g(t)=-2$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}g(t)=4.$"} :step/id #uuid "38507fa3-e58a-5d15-9bed-68d9c6b28a9f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550052}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550046 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d549ab47-43a9-5cd4-8652-3ef960a0d2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549712}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549712} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8648816-420d-52ee-9238-6320b2159f1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186231020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4794af3-fa88-53e1-9a16-3ebffabb89c1" :answer/